# Force LF line endings for files that are executed or parsed on-device.
#
# Android's /system/bin/sh (mksh) cannot handle CRLF: the shebang line becomes
# "#!/system/bin/sh\r" -> interpreter not found / syntax error, and here-docs
# (cat > file <<'EOF') plus line-based grep parsing silently break.
# kr-script XML configs are also read line by line by the on-device reader.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true rewrites the working tree to CRLF on
# every checkout / reset / branch switch, and those CRLF files then get packaged
# straight into APK assets -> scripts fail on the device.
# "eol=lf" pins the working tree to LF and overrides core.autocrlf.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
